{"assets":["/statement-assets/a969b5ceb16bbcb8add9ba826bed9b9e18064700852f48a4084020b8538f9750.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1999","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Showering"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As a computer science student, Alex faces a hard challenge — showering. He tries to shower daily, but despite his best efforts there are always challenges. He takes $$$s$$$ minutes to shower and a day only has $$$m$$$ minutes! "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He already has $$$n$$$ tasks planned for the day. Task $$$i$$$ is represented as an interval $$$(l_i$$$, $$$r_i)$$$, which means that Alex is busy and can not take a shower in that time interval (at any point in time strictly between $$$l_i$$$ and $$$r_i$$$). "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No two tasks overlap."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given all $$$n$$$ time intervals, will Alex be able to shower that day? In other words, will Alex have a free time interval of length at least $$$s$$$?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a969b5ceb16bbcb8add9ba826bed9b9e18064700852f48a4084020b8538f9750.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, Alex can shower for the first $$$3$$$ minutes of the day and not miss any of the tasks."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$s$$$, and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$; $$$1 \\leq s, m \\leq 10^9$$$) — the number of time intervals Alex already has planned, the amount of time Alex takes to take a shower, and the amount of minutes a day has."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then $$$n$$$ lines follow, the $$$i$$$-th of which contains two integers $$$l_i$$$ and $$$r_i$$$ ($$$0 \\leq l_i \\lt r_i \\leq m$$$) — the time interval of the $$$i$$$-th task. No two tasks overlap."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Additional constraint on the input:"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$l_i \\gt r_{i-1}$$$ for every $$$i \\gt 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) if Alex can take a shower for that given test case, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (also without quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in any case (for example, strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as a positive response)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3 3 10\n3 5\n6 8\n9 10\n3 3 10\n1 2\n3 5\n6 7\n3 3 10\n1 2\n3 5\n6 8\n3 4 10\n1 2\n6 7\n8 9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nYES\nNO\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1999C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1999/problem/C"}